(footprint "AXK6S80637YG"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Panasonic AXK6S80637YG, P5KS 0.5mm-pitch 80-pin board-to-board HEADER, 6.0/6.5/9.0mm mated height, with positioning bosses (mates AXK5S80337YG at 9.0mm). No vendor CAD available; built from Panasonic's recommended header pattern (con_eng_p5k.pdf / AXK.pdf: 6.00 outer / 2.00 inner span, 0.25 pads, 0.50 end pads per the bossed pattern on AXK.pdf p.10, 150um stencil 0.23/0.35 x 1.50). Odd pins on the -Y row, pin 1 at -X, so pin n faces socket pin n when AXK5S80337YG is flipped on the mating board. Boss holes 2x 0.65mm NPTH per AXK.pdf p.10 (C = B+1.5 = 21.0, 2.10 apart in Y): (-10.5,+1.05) and (+10.5,-1.05). ASSUMPTION: same pin-1 convention as the AXK5S80337YG socket; confirm against Panasonic's product specification drawing before fab. 3D model is a placeholder box (23.2 x 5.0 x 5.3mm body + bosses), not a vendor model. Pads 2 and 79 (next to the boss holes) are trimmed to start 1.45mm from the centreline (0.5 x 1.55mm) instead of 1.00mm, giving ~0.22mm hole-to-copper instead of Panasonic's 0.05mm; the 150um paste aperture (1.50-3.00mm) is unchanged.")
	(tags "Panasonic P5KS AXK6S80637YG board-to-board 80pin 0.5mm header")
